************************************************************************ File:  StartStop.asm** Copyright Apple Computer, Inc. 1988-92* All Rights Reserved** by Dan Oliver & Steven Glass** This file has two entry points:**    StartupTools*    ShutDownTools** Change History** 02 Nov 88	Dan Oliver** Coding began.** 08 Nov 88	Steven Glass** Integrated with tool locator.  Changed order of tool loading and* shutdown.** Fixed bug for FontManager direct page allocation and startup.** 09 Nov 88	Steven Glass** Changed StartStop record to include flags word and dPage handle.* Flags word can be used later to indicate whether application wants * certain things. (Currently no flags defined.)** DPage hanndle is saved in startstop record at startup so it can* be disposed at shutdown.** Wrote central disposing routine: KillIt to dispose handles.** Returned result of startstop to calling routine by always * copying the handle to result before exit.  This meant * that in the pointer case, I had to put the pointer into* the handle to begin with.** If the shutdown call is called with a handle, we dispose* of it.** 09 Dec 88	Mensch** Added support for Note Synth, Note sequencer, MIDI, and ACE* Modified addPages routine so that it allocates the proper amount of* dpage space when the note seq and sound tools are both started up. * Also, the sound tools startup routine had to be modified to not be  * called when the user wants to use the note seq.** Modified Note synth shutdown and sound tools shutdown so that errors * are ignored. This is so that if you started them up with the noteseq* the shutdown routine will be able to shut everything down.**  01/25/89	Dan - Corrected some comments.** 06 Feb 89	Steven Glass** Added TL to shutdown table.** 06 Feb 89	Harry Yee** Fixed problem in StartTools call. If an error is encountered in starting up* one of the toolsets the stack is not cleaned up correctly. The tool number* is still left on the stack. If an error returns from @StartupTools then an* extra word is pulled off the stack before branching to @errout2.** 10 Feb 89	Harry Yee** In StartTools, we now set the OS global system preferences so that under * certain circumstances, the system's Mount facility will be called to display* a dialog asking the user to mount a specified volume. BRC #41150.** 17 Feb 89	Dave Good** In the start/stop record there a word for the video mode which is passed to* qdstartup and used to determine the mouse clamps for the event manager. The* problem is that there is a new feature in QuickDraw that allows an application* to tell quickdraw to use shadowed memory and this feature uses the high bit* of the video mode. I presume that we want the video mode in the start/stop* record to be used the same way, so I masked it with $00FF in the emStartup* code.** 22 Feb 89	Steven Glass** Changed call to OpenResourceFile to use new inputs.** 03 Mar 89	Dan O** Switched to arrow cursor before leaving StartupTools.  If QDAux was * started the watch cursor was being left.** 14 Mar 89	Steven Glass** Undid dan's fix above.** 30 Mar 89	Steven Glass** Make scrambler safe.  The handle to the start stop record is now* locked before it is used.  It is unlocked just before it is * returned.** 11 Apr 89	Steven Glass** Changed tool number for misc tools.  Was listed as 2, its really 3.** Made it handle all tools except 13.  Any tool not in list is assumed to have* no startup and no direct page needs.** 17-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Currently, TS2 and TS3 both use this whole file.  It might be* possible later to optimize by having TS3 use part of the old ROM* code.** Fixed to start up MidiSynth (#35), Animation (#37) (with 0 Flags and PatchTable),* and Media Control (#38).** Bits 2-15 of startStopRefDesc (startRecFlag) are now ignored, so we can* use them for new things later.** Changed OpenResourceFile stuff to use LGetPathname2 instead of* creating the path "1/"+GET_NAME.** 19-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Defining ShutDownTools bit 2 to be "Don't turn off the graphics* screen," which means we set bit $0100 in SetMasterSCB before calling* QDShutDown.** 20-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Changed StartQuickDraw so that it passes bit $0100 to QDStartUp* if we're going to start up the Window Manager too.  This makes* QD not clear the screen if it's already on.  RefreshDesktop will* get around to clearing the screen eventually.** StartWindowMgr skips the RefreshDesktop call if we're going to* start the Menu Manager too.  StartMenu calls RefreshDesktop.* This gives us a perfectly-smooth app-to-app transition when* possible.** 4-Dec-90	Dave Lyons** AnimStartUp ModeFlag is reall a long, not a word.  Fixed.** 15-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** Implemented bit 0 of the StartStopRecord.Flags word to open the* resource fork "as allowed" instead of always read-only.** 17-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** Changed ShutDownTools to force the leaveScreenOn bit on if it* detects that GQuit's idea of the current application ID is the* same as the current QuickDraw user ID (masked with $F0FF).** 18-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** Oops, my StartUpTools change above is really, really stupid, because* I have no access to that bit before opening the resource file, in* the case that the startup record is referenced by resource.** Instead, StartUpTools startStopRefDesc bit 3 means to open the* resrouce fork as-allowed.** 19-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** Added User ID parameter to AnimStartUp.  Oops.** 21-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** When shutting down the Menu Manager, now I check flag bit 2 to* ShutDownTools; if the bit is clear, I wipe out the menu bar* rectangle before MenuShutDown.** Renamed ShutDownTools flag bit 2 from leaveScreenOn to* leaveScreenIntact.  We have a leaveScreenOn bit internally* that we set if the QD user id matches the GetName user ID.** LeaveScreenIntact means we don't wipe out the menu bar.* (If it's invisible, we don't wipe it out.)** 25-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** If we're starting both QD and EM, the ShowCursor now happens* after EMStartUp instead of after QDStartUp.  This way we don't* see the cursor at the top left of the screen if EMStartUp is* going to put it someplace else.** StartUpTools: flags bit 4 ($0010) avoids starting the Resource* Manager and pre-allocating the super-hires memory.  Intended for* use when it's not your first StartUpTools call, or QD is already* on, or you don't want to start the Resource Manager.** ShutDownTools: flags bit 4 ($0010) avoids shutting down the* Resource Manager.** Including the Resource Manager in the tool record is now a no-op.** 26-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** Whoops, I apparently didn't actually try my previous changes.  Fixed* it so it builds now.** 28-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** Changed value of leaveScreenOn (used internally only) so it doesn't* conflict with any external flag bits.** 21-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Made ShutDownTools call InitCursor.** 30-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Made ShutDownTools call HideCursor instead of InitCursor.** 15-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** ShutDownTools no longer hides the cursor if flag bit 4 is* set ("partial shutdown", skip resource manager stuff, etc).** 19-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** ShutDownTools resets the ShowBootInfo location for drawing icons.** 25-Oct-91	Dave Lyons** Moved a TAX in BuildLoadTable so StartUpTools will work okay for* tools that are bigger than we recognized (will use no parameters* when calling StartUp function).** 17-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** In BuildToolTable, added code to call ReportIfMissing, so that* missing tools show a "This application needs ToolXXX" dialog.************************************************************************* 17-Mar-92	Dave Lyons for 6.0.1** Shutting down Standard File now tolerates errors (in case some* NDA stupidly shut it down during DeskShutDown).** 2-Apr-92	Dave Lyons** ShutDownTools no longer calls HideCursor if QD is inactive.** 1-Jul-92	Dave Lyons** StartUpTools now returns any error from ResourceStartUp.  When* we would have returned garbage for the result, we return NIL.** ShutDownTools:  We check for a NIL input and behave sanely.* ResourceShutDown is now in the error-exit path, so it shuts* down the RM even if you get some other error.***********************************************************************	Blanks off	;No white space in the operand field.		INCLUDE 'all.macros'	include 'e16.memory'************************************************************************   Startup - Shutdown tool equates.***********************************************************************StartStopRecord	Record 0Flags	ds.w 1	Flags for starting and stoppingVideoMode	ds.w 1	SCB byte of mode to	startup in.ResFileID	ds.w 1 	Return file ID of app's res file, NIL = none.DPageHandle	ds.L 1	holds handle allocated for dpageNumTools	ds.w 1  	Number of tools to	load.ToolArray	ds.w 2	Array of tools to load, elements defined as:;		     WORD - tool number.;		     WORD - minimum version number.	ENDR;; --- Direct page offsets.;loading	equ 1	TRUE if loading tools.loadTable	equ loading+2	Load tool hash table, enough for 48 tools.directPages	equ loadTable+6numPages	equ directPages+4getNameBlk	equ numPages+2getName	equ getNameBlk+2getUserID	equ getName+4handle	equ getUserID+2	;added 2nd parameter to GetName, 17-Feb-91 DALptr	equ handle+4UtilFlags	equ ptr+4saveDbank	equ UtilFlags+4	Flags for use with sound tool startup (used Bits 0-3)saveDpage	equ saveDbank+1retAddr	equ saveDpage+2startRec	equ retAddr+6startRecFlag	equ startRec+4userID	equ startRecFlag+2result	equ userID+2leaveScreenIntact	equ 4	;bit 2 for ShutDownTools startRecFlag (DAL)openResReadWrite	equ 8	;(MUST BE BIT 3!) for StartUpTools: open resource fork read/writeskipResMgr	equ $10	;bit 4 for StartUpTools/ShutDownTools: skip RM & pre-allocationleaveScreenOn	equ $20	;bit 5 for ShutDownTools startRecFlag (used internally ONLY!);; --- Tool error codes.;TLBadRecFlag	equ $0103	Invalid startup record flag passed.TLCantLoad	equ $0104	Cant load a tool.;;; --- Tool startup resource equates.;rToolStartup	equ $8013	Resource type of tool startup record.;;; --- UtilFlags codes.WantsSound	equ $0001	indicates sound tools desiredWantsSynth	equ $0002	indicates Note Synth desiredWantsSeq	equ $0004	indicates wants note seuqencer startedWantsMIDI	equ $0008	indicates wants MIDI started;; --- Tool set numbers used;SoundToolSet	equ 8NoteSynth	equ 25NoteSeq	equ 26MIDITools	equ 32; --- System equates.;IncBusyFlg	equ $E10064DecBusyFlg	equ $E10068Stack_Entry	equ $E100B0*****************************************************************StartupTools	PROC EXPORT** Description***   IN: *     PUSH:LONG - space for result.*     PUSH:WORD - User ID.*     PUSH:WORD - 0 if startup record is a pointer, 4 if a resource ID.*     PUSH:LONG - pointer or resource ID of startup record.**  OUT: *     PULL:LONG - handle of startup record if a resource ID was passed, *	else pointer to record.** External Refs:	IMPORT startCall	IMPORT openAppRes	IMPORT getStartupPtr	IMPORT walkToolArray	IMPORT pop	import KillIt** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	jsr startCall		Allocate a direct page.*** added 1-Jul-92 DAL -- Pre-zero the result field so we do not return garbage	stz <result	stz <result+2*** end 1-Jul-92;; Set the global system preferences so that under certain circumstances the; system's Mount facility will be called asking the user to mount a specified volume;; First save the current System Preferences	pea 0	Set up paramBlock for call	pea 1		tsc	calculate address to paramblock	inc a	and push on stack	pea 0	pha	pea $200F	Get_Sys_Prefs	jsl Stack_Entry	Leave parameter block on the stack so we can restore later; Now set the System preferences to display volume mount dialog w/o the cancel button	pea $C000	system preferences	pea 1	pcount	tsc	calculate address to paramblock	inc a	and push on stack	pea 0		pha	pea $200C	Set_Sys_Prefs	jsr Stack_Entry	pla	Get Parameter block off the stack.	pla;;; --- Open application's resource file.;	jsr openAppRes		Open application's resource file.*** added 1-Jul-92 DAL -- check for bad error	bcs @toErrOut		;Y = error if SEC*** end 1-Jul-92	pha 		Save open resource file ID.	jsr getStartupPtr		Get startup record pointer.	pla	bcc @ok1		Error?  Y = error code.@toErrOut	brl @errOut@ok1	ldy #StartStopRecord.ResFileID	Return file ID of app's open resource file.	sta [<startRec],y;;; --- Allocate direct pages for tools.;	stz <numPages		Start with no pages.	stz <UtilFlags		zero out the flags;	lda #addPages		Compute number of direct pages needed.	jsr walkToolArray;	lda <numPages		Any direct pages needed?	beq @skip1;	lda #0		Common need.	pha 		Space for result.	pha	pha 		Pass number of bytes to allocate.	pei <numPages	pei <userID		Pass my user ID.	pea $C005		Pass attributes; locked, fixed bank, page aligned.	pha 		Pass address, bank zero.	pha	_NewHandle	tay 		Possible error code.	pla	sta <directPages	pla	sta <directPages+2	bcs @toErrOut;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Put direct page handle into the startstop record.;	ldy #StartStopRecord.DPageHandle	lda directPages	sta [StartRec],y	iny	iny	lda directPages+2	sta [StartRec],y;;; --- Load and start tools requested by	caller.;@skip1		stz <loadTable		Clear tool load table.	stz <loadTable+2	stz <loadTable+4;	stz <loading		TRUE for loading tools.	inc <loading;	lda #0	pha	pha*** added 25-Feb-91 DAL	lda <startRecFlag	and #skipResMgr	bne @skipPreallocate	;if we skip, there is a NIL handle on the stack*** end of 25-Feb-91 DAL	PushLong #$00008000	PushWord #$4001		; tool locator's user id	PushWord #attrAddr	PushLong #$00E12000	_NewHandle@skipPreallocate	lda #buildLoadTable		Build hash table of	tools to load.	jsr walkToolArray	pla		Get handle to screen into	plx		a & X	php		Save error status	phy		Save error code	jsr KillIt	ply		Restore error code and	plp		status register	bcc @ok2		Error loading tools?;	tya@errOut2	pha 		Save error code.	ldx <directPages+2		Free allocated direct pages.	lda <directPages	jsr KillIt	ply 		Restore error code.	brl @errOut;@ok2	stz <numPages		Start with first page.;; --- Startup loop.;	ldx #0	bra @enter1@lop1	phx	jsr checkLoadTable		Check if user wants	this tool started.	beq @next1	lda 1,s		Call startup handler.	tax	jsr (@startupTable+1,x)	bcc @next1		No error?	plx		Error, so clean up stack and beat it.	bra @errOut2@next1	plx 		Next tool.	inx	inx	inx@enter1	lda |@startupTable,x 	Next tool to start.	and #$00FF	bne @lop1		Any more tools?;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Return the result to the calling routine.;	lda handle	sta Result	lda handle+2	sta Result+2;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Unlock if input was handle or resource;;	lda StartRecFlag	and #3	;bits 0-1	(added 17-Nov-90 DAL)	beq @IsPtr	ldy #4	lda [<handle],y;	and #$7FFF	asl a	lsr a	sta [<handle],y@IsPtr	ldy #0	No error.@errOut	tsc	Parameter block for Set_Sys_Prefs still on stack	inc a	pea 0000	pha	pea $200C	jsl Stack_Entry	plx	Get parameter block off the stack.	plx;; --- Exit.;;  y = error code.;	ldx #8	Number of bytes to strip.	brl pop************************************************************************ This is the startup table.  To add a	tool to be started up add* a record to this table at the position you want it to be started.* The first tool started is the first tool in the table.* A record is a one byte tool number followed by a one word* address of a routine that starts the tool.  The routine should * start the tool and return carry set if there is an error with* an error code in	a.***********************************************************************	IMPORT startMiscTools	IMPORT startQuickDraw	IMPORT startQDAux	IMPORT startEventMgr	IMPORT startWindowMgr	IMPORT startControlMgr	IMPORT startMenuMgr	IMPORT startDialog	IMPORT startLineEdit	IMPORT startStandardFile	IMPORT startDeskMgr	IMPORT startScrap	IMPORT startSound	IMPORT startSANE	IMPORT startPrintMgr	IMPORT startFont	IMPORT startTextEdit	IMPORT startNoteSynth	IMPORT StartNoteSeq	IMPORT startMIDI	IMPORT startACE	import startPokey	import startAnimation	;added 17-Nov-90 DAL	import startMediaCtl	;added 17-Nov-90 DAL	import startMidiSynth	;added 17-Nov-90 DAL	import startResMgr		;26-Feb-91 DAL@startupTable	dc.b 3	dc.w startMiscTools	dc.b 4	dc.w startQuickDraw	dc.b 18	dc.w startQDAux	dc.b 6	dc.w startEventMgr	dc.b 14	dc.w startWindowMgr	dc.b 16	dc.w startControlMgr	dc.b 15	dc.w startMenuMgr	dc.b 20	dc.w startLineEdit	dc.b 21	dc.w startDialog	dc.b 22	dc.w startScrap	dc.b 23	dc.w startStandardFile	dc.b 27	dc.w startFont	dc.b 19	dc.w startPrintMgr	dc.b 34	dc.w startTextEdit	dc.b 8	dc.w startSound	dc.b NoteSynth	dc.W startNoteSynth	dc.b NoteSeq	dc.W StartNoteSeq	dc.b MIDITools	dc.W StartMIDI	dc.b 29	dc.W startACE	dc.b 10	dc.w startSANE	dc.b 33	dc.w startPokey	dc.b 35		;added 17-Nov-90 DAL	dc.w startMidiSynth		;added 17-Nov-90 DAL	dc.b 37		;added 17-Nov-90 DAL	dc.w startAnimation		;added 17-Nov-90 DAL	dc.b 38		;added 17-Nov-90 DAL	dc.w startMediaCtl		;added 17-Nov-90 DAL	dc.b 5	dc.w startDeskMgr	dc.b $1E		;added 25-Feb-91 DAL	dc.w startResMgr		;added 25-Feb-91 DAL (no-op)	dc.b 0		;No more tools.;-----------------------------------------------------;   Compute number of direct pages needed.;-----------------------------------------------------;;   IN: y = index to tool in startup record.;   a = tool number.;   <numPages = current number of direct pages needed.;addPages	cmp #endTools-toolTable Tool number in range?	bcs @exit	tay	place the tool number in <Y>;; First test to see if this is one of the sound tools	ldx #0	use <X> as a temp flag	cmp #SoundToolSet	is this the sound tools?	bne @AP0010	if not test for note synth	lda #WantsSound	load the proper flag	bra @SetFlag	and set it@AP0010	cmp #NoteSynth	is it the Note synthesizer?	bne @AP0020	if not test for MIDI	lda #WantsSynth	load the proper flag	bra @SetFlag	and set it@AP0020	cmp #MIDITools	is it the MIDI Tools?	bne @AP0030	if not test for Note Sequencer	lda #WantsMIDI	tax	set <X> flag to be true	bra @SetFlag@AP0030	cmp #NoteSeq	is it the note sequencer?	bne @DoAdd	if not, just add in the proper value	lda #WantsSeq	load the proper flag	tax	and set our <X>flag to be true; The SetFlag routine sets the proper flag in the UtilFlags word for the tool; and then checks to see if the Note sequencer has already been added, If so, ; we will skip adding more direct page space for the tools.@SetFlag	ora <UtilFlags	set the flag	sta <UtilFlags	cpx #00	test <X> for zero	bne @AddSeq	if its non-zero we are adding the sequencer or MIDI	and #WantsSeq	next test if they already added sequencer direct page	bne @Exit	if so, then we no longer need to add direct page; Now add the standard direct page value@DoAdd	lda |toolTable,y 	Get pages this tool needs.	and #$007F	xba	clc	adc <numPages	Increment total pages needed.	sta <numPages;@exit	clc 	Continue flag.	rts; Add the sequencer direct page, but first test to see if the other tools have; already been added.@AddSeq	lda <UtilFlags	get the flags	tax	save it for later	and #WantsSound	test to see if sound already added in	bne @AS0010	if not the test for MIDI	dec <numPages-1	decrement the number of pages by 1@AS0010	bra @DoAdd	if not, go ahead and add the proper number of pages	canLoad	equ $0080	TRUE if I can load this tool.	ENTRY toolTabletoolTable	dc.b 0	0 - not used.	dc.b canLoad+0	1 - Tool Locator, startup not needed.	dc.b canLoad+0	2 - Memory Manager,	started by application.	dc.b canLoad+0	3 - Misc. Tool set.	dc.b canLoad+3	4 - QuickDraw II.	dc.b canLoad+0	5 - Desk Manager.	dc.b canLoad+1	6 - Event Manger.	dc.b canLoad+0	7 - Scheduler, startup not needed.	dc.b canLoad+1	8 - Sound tool set.	dc.b canLoad+0	9 - Apple Desktop Bus Tool set, startup	not needed.	dc.b canLoad+1	10 - SANE	dc.b canLoad+0	11 - Integer Math tool set, startup not	needed.	dc.b canLoad+0	12 - Text tool set,	startup not needed.	dc.b 0	13 - not used.	dc.b canLoad+0	14 - Window Manager.	dc.b canLoad+1	15 - Menu Manager.	dc.b canLoad+1	16 - Control Manager.	dc.b canLoad+0	17 - System Loader,	startup not needed.	dc.b canLoad+0	18 - QuickDraw Auxiliary.	dc.b canLoad+2	19 - Print Manager.	dc.b canLoad+1	20 - LineEdit	dc.b canLoad+0	21 - Dialog Manager.	dc.b canLoad+0	22 - Scrap Manager.	dc.b canLoad+1	23 - Standard File Operations.	dc.b canLoad+0	24 - future Tool.	dc.b canLoad+0	25 - Note synthesizer.	dc.b canLoad+3	26 - Note sequencer.	dc.b canLoad+1	27 - Font Manager.	dc.b canLoad+0	28 - List Manager, startup not needed.	dc.b canLoad+1	29 - ACE	dc.b canLoad+0	30 - Resource Manager, startup always happens.	dc.b canLoad+0	31 - not used.	dc.b canLoad+3	32 - MIDI	dc.b canLoad+0	33 - Pokey	dc.b canLoad+1	34 - Text edit.	dc.b canLoad+0	35 - MidiSynth	(added 17-Nov-90 DAL)	dc.b 0	36 - not used	(added 17-Nov-90 DAL)	dc.b canLoad+1	37 - Animation	(added 17-Nov-90 DAL)	dc.b canLoad+0	38 - Media Control	(added 17-Nov-90 DAL)endTools************************************************************************   Load tool.***   IN: *        y 	= index to tool in startup record.*        a 	= tool number.*        <numPages 	= next available direct page.*        <loading 	= TRUE to load tools.**  OUT:  Carry set if error, y = error code.***********************************************************************	import ReportIfMissing	entry buildLoadTablebuildLoadTable	tax		;25-Oct-91 DAL	cmp #endTools-toolTable	Tool number in range?	bcs @OkToTry;;;	tax		;moved above 25-Oct-91 DAL	lda |toolTable,x		;Is there a loader for the tool?	and #$00FF	beq @cantError@OkToTry;	lda <loading		Am I loading tools?	beq @skip1;	phx 		Save tool number.;	phx 		Pass tool number.	iny	iny	lda [<startRec],y		Pass minimum tool version.	pha	_LoadOneTool	tay 		Possible error code.	plx 		Restore tool number.	bcc @skip1*** added 17-Dec-91 DAL -- put up an alert saying they need the tool	phy	txa	;tool # in A	tyx	;error in X for ReportIfMissing	jsr ReportIfMissing	ply	;error code	sec*** end 17-Dec-91	rts 	Abort.@skip1	txa 	Compute index to bit in LoadTable.	and #$0007	tay;	txa	lsr a	lsr a	lsr a	tax;	sep #$20	Set bit in hash table for tool to be loaded.	LONGA OFF	lda <loadTable,x	ora |loadMasks,y	sta <loadTable,x	rep #$20	LONGA ON;	clc 	Continue flag.	rts;@cantError	ldy #TLCantLoad	Error code.	sec	rts;loadMasks	dc.b $80,$40,$20,$10,$08,$04,$02,$01************************************************************************   Check loadTable	if tool should be loaded.***   IN: a 	= tool number, already checked for being in range.*       <loadTable 	= pointer to load table.***********************************************************************	entry checkLoadTablecheckLoadTable	pha	and #$0007	tay	pla	lsr a	lsr a	lsr a	tax	sep #$20	LONGA OFF	lda <loadTable,x	and |loadMasks,y	rep #$20	LONGA ON	rts	ENDP*****************************************************************ShutdownTools	PROC EXPORT**   If handle of startup record is passed the handle is disposed of.***   IN: *     PUSH:WORD - 0 if startup record is a pointer, 2 if a handle.*     PUSH:LONG - pointer or handle of startup record.**  OUT: *     Nothing.** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:	IMPORT startCall	IMPORT getStartupPtr	IMPORT checkLoadTable	IMPORT walkToolArray	import KillIt	IMPORT StopNoteSynth	IMPORT StopSound	import StopMM	import stopQuickDraw	import stopMenuMgr	import stopResMgr		;26-Feb-91 DAL	import stopStdFile		;17-Mar-92 DAL*** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	jsr startCall	;Allocate a direct page.*** added 1-Jul-92 DAL -- If tool table reference is NIL, use a clean by-pointer table	lda <startRec+2	ora <startRec	bne @notNIL	lda #@defaultStopRecord>>16	ldx #@defaultStopRecord	sta <startRec+2	stx <startRec	stz <handle	stz <handle+2	lda #3	trb <startRecFlag	;force it to be a pointer	bra @ok1@defaultStopRecord	dc.w 0	;flags	dc.w 0	;QD masterSCB	dc.w 0	;resFileID	dc.l 0	;direct page handle	dc.w 0	;tool count@notNIL*** end 1-Jul-92	jsr getStartupPtr	;Get startup record pointer.	bcc @ok1	;Error?  Y = error code.	brl @errOut@ok1	stz <loadTable	;Clear tool load table.	stz <loadTable+2	stz <loadTable+4	pea $8000	lda #0	pha	;StringPtr = $80000000	pha	pha	;IconPtr = nil	_ShowBootInfo	;initialize ShowBootInfo!	lda <startRecFlag	;added 15-Sep-91 DAL	and #skipResMgr	;	bne @skipHide	;(fixes bug 1009954)*** added 2-Apr-92 DAL -- Don't call HideCursor if QD is not started (6.0.1)	pha	_QDStatus	pla	beq @skipHide*** end 2-Apr-92	_HideCursor@skipHide*** Force the leaveScreenOn bit on in the flags if GetName says*** the user ID matches ours.	lda #2	sta <getNameBlk	;GetNameGS with 2 parameters	tsc	;built a 32-character filename result buffer on the stack	sec	sbc #36	;space for filename buffer	tcs	inc a	sta <getName	stz <getName+2	lda #36	sta 1,s	;store buffer size in first word	pea 0	tdc	clc	adc #getNameBlk	pha	pea $2027	;GetNameGS	jsl $e100b0	;stack OS entry	bcs @err	pha	pha	;space for GetWAP result	pea 0	;system tool	pea 4	;QuickDraw II	_GetWAP	plx	pla*** added 17-Feb-92 DAL for 6.0.1d1 -- If QD isn't started, don't check bogus zpage value	txa	beq @differentID*** end 17-Feb-92	lda >$00000A,x	;QuickDraw user ID	and #$f0ff	;master ID	cmp <getUserID	bne @differentID	lda #leaveScreenOn	tsb <startRecFlag	;force the bit on@differentID@err	tsc	clc	adc #36	tcs*** end of leaveScreenOn code	stz <loading		;FALSE for no loading.	lda #buildLoadTable		;Build hash table of tools that were loaded.	jsr walkToolArray;-----------------------------------------------------------; ; Shutdown loop.;	ldx #0	bra @enter1@lop1	phx;	jsr checkLoadTable		Check if user wants	this tool started.	clc 		Make flag correct.	beq @next1;	plx		Call shutdown handler.	phx	lda |shutdownTable+1,x 	Is there a handler?	bne @ok2;	lda |shutdownTable,x	Compute shutdown call number.	and #$00FF	ora #$0300	tax	jsl $E10000		Call tool's shutdown, no parameters.	bra @enter2;@ok2	jsr (shutdownTable+1,x)@enter2	tay		Possible error code into y.@next1	plx	bcs @errOut		Error?;	inx		Next tool.	inx	inx@enter1	lda |shutdownTable,x 	Next tool to shutdown.	and #$00FF	bne @lop1		Any more tools?;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Dispose of the handle we allocated for direct page.;	ldy #StartStopRecord.DPageHandle+2	lda [startrec],y	tax	dey	dey	lda [startrec],y	jsr KillIt;-----------------------------------------------------------;; If the input to this call is a handle, dispose of it.;	lda <StartRecFlag	and #3	;17-Nov-90 DAL	beq @NotHandle	lda <handle	ldx <handle+2	jsr KillIt@NotHandle;-----------------------------------------------------------;; We log off the res mgr last just in case any of the; other tools need the res mgr to shut down.;;;;	lda <startRecFlag;;;	and #skipResMgr;;;	bne @skipRMSD;;;	_ResourceShutdown	;Log off of Resource Manager.;;;@skipRMSD	ldy #0	;No error.;; @errOut -- Exit;@errOut*** 1-Jul-92 DAL -- Moved ResourceShutDown code here (in error-exit path)	phy	;save error code	lda <startRecFlag	and #skipResMgr	bne @skipRMSD	_ResourceShutDown@skipRMSD	ply	;restore error code*** end 1-Jul-92	ldx #6	;Number of bytes to strip.	entry poppop	jsl DecBusyFlg;; --- Restore saved	parameters from startupCall.;;	tsc 	;Free allocate direct page in stack.	clc	adc #saveDbank-1	tcs	plb 	;Restore original data bank.;; --- Move return addresses over top of	input parameters.;	tsc	tcd	lda 7,s	sta 7,x	lda 5,s	sta 5,x	lda 3,s	sta 3,x;; --- Adjust stact for popped parameters.;	pld 	;Get original direct page pointer.	tsc 	;Current stack,	phx	clc	adc 1,s	;plus number of bytes popped,	tcs 	;equals new stack.	tya 	;Return error code in Y.	cmp #1	;Set carry if error.	rtl************************************************************************ This is the shutdown table.  To add a tool to be shutdown * add a record to this table at the position you want it to be shutdown.* The first tool shutdown is the first tool in the table.* A record is a one byte tool number followed by a one word * address of a routine that shutdown the tool or zero to just call * its shutdown call.  The routine should shutdown the tool and * return carry set if there is an error with an error code in a.** Change History** 06 Feb 89	Steven Glass** Added tool locator to end of list.** 17-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Added Media Control, Animation, MidiSynth right after Desk Manager.***********************************************************************shutdownTable		dc.b 5	;Desk Mgr	dc.w 0	dc.b 38	;Media Control	(added 17-Nov-90 DAL)	dc.w 0		(added 17-Nov-90 DAL)	dc.b 37	;Animation	(added 17-Nov-90 DAL)	dc.w 0		(added 17-Nov-90 DAL)	dc.b 35	;MidiSynth	(added 17-Nov-90 DAL)	dc.w 0		(added 17-Nov-90 DAL)	dc.b 33	;Video Overlay	dc.w 0	dc.b 10	;SANE	dc.w 0	dc.b 29	;ACE	dc.W 0	dc.b NoteSeq	;Note sequencer	dc.W 0	dc.B MIDITools	;MIDI	dc.W 0	dc.B NoteSynth	;Note Synth	dc.W StopNoteSynth	dc.b 8	;Sound Tool	dc.w StopSound	dc.b 34	;Text Edit	dc.w 0	dc.b 19	;Print Mgr	dc.w 0	dc.b 27	;Font Mgr	dc.w 0	dc.b 23	;Standard File	dc.w stopStdFile	dc.b 21	;Dialog Mgr	dc.w 0	dc.b 22	;Scrap Mgr	dc.w 0	dc.b 20	;Line Edit	dc.w 0	dc.b 15	;Menu Mgr	dc.w stopMenuMgr	dc.b 16	;Control Mgr	dc.w 0	dc.b 14	;Window Manager	dc.w 0	dc.b 6	;Event Mgr	dc.w 0	dc.b 18	;QD Aux	dc.w 0	dc.b 4	;Quick Draw	dc.w stopQuickDraw	dc.b 3	;Misc. Tools	dc.w 0	dc.b 2	;Memory Manager	dc.w StopMM	dc.b $1E	;Resource Manager 25-Feb-91 DAL	dc.w StopResMgr	; (no-op)	dc.b 1	;Tool Locator	dc.w 0	dc.b 0	;(No more tools)	ENDP*****************************************************************getStartupPtr	PROC** Description*** Inputs:*	none** Outputs:*        <handle = handle of startup record, NIL if none.*        <startRec = pointer to startup record.*        Carry set if error, y = error code.** External Refs:	IMPORT derefHand** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************;;;	ldy #TLBadRecFlag	;Possible error code.	lda <startRecFlag	;Dispatch to converter.	and #3	;17-Nov-90 DAL	asl a	tax;;;	cpx #5;;;	bcs @errOut	jmp (@converters,x)@converters	dc.w @pointer	dc.w @hand	dc.w @res*** added 1-Jul-92 DAL	dc.w @illegal@illegal	ldy #TLBadRecFlag	sec	rts*** end 1-Jul-92;;; ------ Startup record is a handle.;@hand	lda <startRec	;Save handle.	ldx <startRec+2	sta <handle	stx <handle+2	brl derefHand	;<startRec = (<handle);;; ------ Startup record is a resource ID.;@res	pha 	;Space for result.	pha	pea rToolStartup	;Pass resource type of resource startup record.	pei <startRec+2	;Pass resource ID of resource startup record.	pei <startRec	_LoadResource	tay	;Put possible error code in y.	pla	plx	bcs @errOut;	sta <handle	stx <handle+2;	pea rToolStartup	;Pass resource type of resource startup record.	pei <startRec+2	;Pass resource ID of resource startup record.	pei <startRec	_DetachResource	;Let startup record float.;	brl derefHand	;<startRec = (<handle);;; ------ Startup record is a pointer.;@pointer	lda startRec	No handle so copy pointer to handle to use	sta <handle	as output	lda startRec+2	sta <handle+2	clc 	No error.@errOut	rts	ENDP*****************************************************************startCall	PROC** Incs the busy flag, and gets d-page off stack for use* in call.*** Inputs:*	none** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************;	jsl IncBusyFlg;	plx 	Get caller's return address.;	phd 	Save caller's direct page pointer.	phb 	Save caller's data bank pointer.	phk	plb;	tsc 	Allocate direct page in stack.	sec	sbc #saveDbank-1	tcs	tcd;	phx 	Put return address back.	rts	ENDP*****************************************************************derefHand	PROC** Derefernce handle of startup record	if there is a handle.*** Inputs:*	handle** Outputs:*	startRec** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************;	lda <handle+1	NIL handle?	beq @exit;	ldy #4	Lock the handle  (added 30 Mar 89)	lda [<handle],y	ora #$8000	sta [<handle],y	ldy #2	Dereference the handle.	lda [<handle],y	sta <startRec+2	lda [<handle]	sta <startRec;@exit	clc 	No error.	rts	ENDP*****************************************************************openAppRes	PROC** Open the application's resource fork.*** Inputs:*	direct page stuff** Outputs:*	a-reg = openfile id, NIL if none*                   SEC = bad error (in Y) (added 1-Jul-92)** External Refs:	import KillIt** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on******************************************************************** added 25-Feb-91 DAL	lda <startRecFlag	and #skipResMgr	beq @doResMgr	brl @errOut@doResMgr*** end of 25-Feb-91 DAL	pha 	;Is the Resource Manager loaded?	_ResourceStatus	pla	bcc @1	brl @errOut@1	pei <userID	;Pass user ID.	_ResourceStartUp	;Log application in with Resource Manager.*** added 1-Jul-92 DAL -- Check for an error from ResourceStartUp	bcc @resStarted	tay;	sec	rts@resStarted*** end 1-Jul-92;; ------ Get name of application.;	pha 	;Space for result.	pha	pea 0	;Pass number of bytes to allocate.	pea 1024	pei <userID	;Pass user ID.	pea $C000	;Pass attributes, fixed.	pha	;Pass address, not used.	pha	_NewHandle	plx	stx <handle	plx	stx <handle+2	tay 	;Possible error code.	bcs @errOut	ldy #2	;Dereference the handle.	lda [<handle],y	sta <getName+2	lda [<handle]	sta <getName*** The old way:  use "1/" + GetName (17-Nov-90 DAL)*** old way	;*** old way		lda #1024	Size of name buffer.*** old way		sta [<getName]*** old way	;*** old way		lda #1	Initialize parameter block.*** old way		sta <getNameBlk*** old way	;*** old way		pea 0	Pass pointer to parameter block.*** old way		tdc*** old way		clc*** old way		adc #getNameBlk*** old way		pha*** old way		pea $2027	GetName.*** old way		jsl $E100B0	Call GS/OS to get the name of the appliation.*** old way	;*** old way		ldy #2	Get length of name,*** old way		lda [<getName],y*** old way		inc a	add size of prefix to be added,*** old way		inc a*** old way		sta [<getName]	turn into an input name.*** old way	;*** old way		lda #$2F31	Add application prefix '1/'*** old way		sta [<getName],y*** old way	*** old way	*** old way	; Let me take a moment to say how much fun it is to*** old way	; get the application's pathname.  And soooo easy too!*** The New Way:  Use LGetPathname2 on the master UserID passed in	pha	pha	;space for LGetPathname2 result	lda <UserID	and #$f0ff	pha	pea 1	;file number	_LGetPathname2	pla	;anticipate error:	bcs @pathError	;take branch with ONE word to be pulled	pha	;put half of result back on stack	phd	tsc	tcd	lda [3]	;get length of pathname	inc a	inc a	pld* leave LGetPathname2 result on stack for BlockMove	pei <getName+2	;destination for BlockMove	pei <getName	pea 0	pha	;length of string	_BlockMove;; ------ Open application's resource file.;	pha 	;Space for OpenResourceFile result***	PushWord #1	;Read only access!*** 15,18-Feb-91 DAL -- bit 3 of the StartStopRefRef means open res fork "as allowed" instead of read-only	lda <startRecFlag	and #openResReadWrite	lsr a	lsr a	lsr a	eor #1	pha*** end of 15,18-Feb-91 DAL	lda #0	;Pass map pointer, none.	pha	pha	pei <getName+2	;Pass pointer to GS/OS input name of application.	pei <getName	_OpenResourceFile@pathError	php 	;Save result.	ldx <handle+2	;Free pathname buffer.	lda <handle	jsr KillIt	plp 	;Restore status.	pla	;Get file ID returned by OpenResource (or 2nd word of LGetPathname2 result)	bcc @exit@errOut	lda #0	;Return no open file ID.@exit	clc	;always return from here with CLC, started ResMgr (1-Jul-92)	rts	ENDP*****************************************************************walkToolArray	PROC** Calls the indicated routine for each tool in the array.  The* indicated routine is called with following inputs:**	y = index to tool in startup record** The output from the routine is the carry flag: set to abort.***   IN: *      a = 	address of routine to call for each tool in the array.*      <startRec = 	pointer to start record that contains the tool array.**  OUT: *      Carry set if routine aborted walk.*      Carry clear if entire list walk.*** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************@saveToolIndex	equ 1@saveToolCounter	equ @saveToolIndex+2@routine	equ @saveToolCounter+2	dec a	;Make address a return address.	pha	;Save address.	ldy #StartStopRecord.NumTools	;Get number of tools in array.	lda [<startRec],y	tax	iny	;Index to first tool.	iny	bra @enter1@lop1	phx	;Save tool counter.	phy	;Save tool index.	lda @routine,s	pea @return-1	;Put return address on stack.	pha 	;Dispatch to routine to call.	lda [<startRec],y	;Pass tool number.	rts@return	pla	plx	bcs @exit	;Did routine abort?	clc	;Increment index to next tool element.	adc #4	tay@enter1	dex	;Any more tools?	bpl @lop1	clc	;Entire array walked flag.@exit	pla	;Get rid of return address.	rts	ENDP;=====================================================================;   Pass pointer to	direct page and increment counter.;=====================================================================;;   IN: a = tool number, range already checked.;   <directPages = handle of direct pages.;   <numPages = next available direct page.;;  OUT: Pointer to available direct page on stack.;   <numPages = next available direct page.;pushDirectPage	PROC	IMPORT toolTable	tay 	;Save tool number.	plx 	;Pull return address.	lda [<directPages]	;Push pointer to next available direct page.	clc	adc <numPages	pha	phx 	;Put return address back.	lda |toolTable,y	;Increment page counter.	and #$007F	xba	clc	adc <numPages	sta <numPages	rts	ENDP;*************************************************************************************;           Tool Startup handlers.;*************************************************************************************;===========================================;   Start Miscellaneous Tools.;===========================================startMiscTools	PROC	_MTStartup	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start QuickDraw.;===========================================startQuickDraw	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	lda #4		;Pass address of QuickDraw's direct pages.	jsr pushDirectPage	ldy #StartStopRecord.VideoMode	;Pass video mode to start in.	lda [<startRec],y	pha*** added 20-Nov-90 DAL: If we're starting the Window Manager too, don't clear the screen	lda #14	;window manager	jsr checkLoadTable	beq @noWM	pla	ora #$0100	;force bit $0100 on in the MasterSCB word	pha@noWM*** end of 20-Nov-90 DAL	pea 160	;Pass bytes per scan line.	pei <userID	;Pass user ID.	_QDStartup	bcs @errOut2*** added 25-Feb-91 DAL: If we're starting the Event Mgr too, don't show the cursor yet	lda #6	jsr checkLoadTable	bne @doingEM***	_ShowCursor 	;Turn on cursor.@doingEM	clc@errOut2	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start QuickDraw	Aux.;===========================================startQDAux	PROC	_QDAuxStartup	_WaitCursor	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Event Manager.;===========================================startEventMgr	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	lda  #6		;pointer to Event Manager direct page.	jsr  pushDirectPage	pea  20		;queue size.	pea  0		;minimum x mouse clamp.	ldx  #640	ldy  #StartStopRecord.VideoMode	;video mode to start in.	lda  [<startRec],y***	and  #$00FF		;Added by DDG to fix shadowed QD bug	and #$0080		;changed from $ff to $80 17-Nov-90 DAL	bne  @okEM	ldx  #320@okEM	phx		;maximum x mouse clamp.	pea  0		;minimum y mouse clamp.	pea  200		;maximum y mouse clamp.	pei  <userID		;application's user ID.	_EMStartup	bcs @outtahere*** 25-Feb-91 DAL: If we started QD too, do a ShowCursor now	lda #4	jsr checkLoadTable	beq @noQD	_ShowCursor@noQD	clc***@outtahere	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Window Manager.;===========================================startWindowMgr	PROC	pei <userID	;Pass application's user ID.	_WindStartup	bcs @toerrOut2	lda #15	;Menu Manager too?   21-Nov-90 DAL	jsr checkLoadTable	; (Refresh *after* MenuStartUp if we can!)	clc	;	bne @toerrOut2	;	pea 0	;Pass 'entire screen' flag.	pea 0	_RefreshDesktop 	;Draw screen.@toerrOut2	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Control Manager.;===========================================startControlMgr	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	pei <userID	;Pass application's user ID.	lda #16	;Pass pointer to Control Manager direct page.	jsr pushDirectPage	_CtlStartup	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Menu Manager.;===========================================startMenuMgr	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	pei <userID	;Pass application's user ID.	lda #15	;Pass pointer to direct page.	jsr pushDirectPage	_MenuStartup	bcs @1	pea 0	;added 21-Nov-90 DAL	pea 0	_RefreshDesktop@1	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Dialog Manager.;===========================================startDialog	PROC	pei <userID	;Pass application's user ID.	_DialogStartup	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Line Edit.;===========================================startLineEdit	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	pei <userID	;Pass application's user ID.	lda #20	;Pass pointer to direct page.	jsr pushDirectPage	_LEStartup	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Standard File.;===========================================startStandardFile	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	pei <userID	;Pass application's user ID.	lda #23	;Pass pointer to direct page.	jsr pushDirectPage	_SFStartup	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Desk Manager.;===========================================startDeskMgr	PROC	_DeskStartup	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Resource Manager (no-op);===========================================startResMgr	PROC	clc	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Scrap Manager.;===========================================startScrap	PROC	_ScrapStartup	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Sound Tool.;	8 dec 88 Modified to check for note seq startup - Mensch;===========================================startSound	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	lda <UtilFlags	;first test to see if we are going to start the seq	and #WantsSeq		bne @done	;if so, then skip NoteSynth startup	lda #8	;Pass pointer to direct page.	jsr pushDirectPage	_SoundStartup@done	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Note Synth Tool.;	8 dec 88 Added - Mensch;===========================================startNoteSynth	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	lda <UtilFlags	;first test to see if we are going to start the seq	and #WantsSeq		bne @done	;if so, then skip NoteSynth startup		lda #0	pha	;default update rate	pha	;no user update rtn	pha	_NSStartUp@done	rts	ENDP;============================================;    Stop QuickDraw;	19-Nov-90 Dave Lyons -- added;; Calls QDShutDown, but first we set bit $0100; of the MasterSCB if we should leave the SHR; screen turned on.;;============================================stopQuickDraw	proc	lda <startRecFlag	and #leaveScreenOn+leaveScreenIntact	beq @1	pha	_GetMasterSCB	pla	ora #$0100	pha	_SetMasterSCB	pha	_GetMasterSCB	_SetAllSCBS	;experimental 21-Nov-90 DAL (Andy N was whining for this)	_HideCursor@1	_QDShutDown	rts;============================================;    Stop Menu Manager;	21-Feb-91 Dave Lyons -- added;; Checks the leaveScreenIntact flag in startRecFlag.; If clear, we wipe out the menu bar before; calling MenuShutDown.;;============================================stopMenuMgr	proc	lda <startRecFlag	and #leaveScreenIntact	bne @noWipe	pha	pha	_GetPort	;preserve old port	pha	pha	_GetMenuMgrPort	_SetPort	;set menu manager port	pha	pha	_GetSysBar	phd	;dereference system menu bar handle	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [3],y	tax	lda [3]	clc	;add 8 (offset to rectangle)	adc #8	sta 3	bcc @1	inx@1	stx 5	;deference system menu bar	ldy #8	;offset past rectangle to flags	lda [3],y	and #$0080	;menu bar invisible?	bne @menuBarInvis	ldy #6@pushrect	lda [3],y	pha	dey	dey	bpl @pushrect	tsc	inc a	pea 0	pha	;pushed rectangle pointer for EraseRect	pea 0	pha	;push rectangle pointer again for InsetRect	pea 2	;horizontal inset	pea 1	;vertical inset	_InsetRect	_EraseRect	pla	pla	pla	pla	;pulled rectangle@menuBarInvis	pld	;restore direct page	pla	pla	;pull dereferenced value	_SetPort	;restore old port@nowipe	_MenuShutDown	rts;============================================;    Stop MM (Memory Manager).;	11 Apr 89 added - Glass; Does nothing.;============================================StopResMgr	proc	EndPStopMM	PROC	rts	ENDP;============================================; Stop Standard File;   New routine 17-Mar-92 DAL to tolerate error;============================================stopStdFile	proc	_SFShutDown	clc	rts	EndP;============================================;    Stop Note synth Tool.;	9 dec 88 added - Mensch;============================================StopNoteSynth	Proc	_NSShutDown	;shut down note synth and ignore errors	clc	;they mean nothing since only error is not started	rts;============================================;    Stop Sound Tools;	9 dec 88 added - mensch;============================================StopSound	Proc	_SoundShutDown	;ignore errors here	clc	rts;===========================================;   Start MIDI tools.;	8 dec 88 Added - Mensch;===========================================startMIDI	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	pei <userID	;Pass application's user ID.	lda #32	;Pass pointer to direct page.	jsr pushDirectPage	_MIDIStartup	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start NOTE sequencer.;	8 dec 88 Added - Mensch;===========================================startNoteSeq	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	lda #26	;Pass pointer to direct page.	jsr pushDirectPage	lda <UtilFlags	;see if the user wanted MIDI started up	and #WantsMIDI		beq @SNS0010	;if not then just push a zero for MODE	lda #$8000	;if MIDI then set high bit of MODE@SNS0010	pha	;push the mode	pea $0000	;use the standard update rate	pea #20	;use 20 as the standard increment	_SeqStartup	bcs @SNSErr	_StopInts	;turn off sequencer interupts for now@SNSErr	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start ACE.;	8 dec 88 added - Mensch;===========================================startACE	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage*** Note that this doesn't call ACEInfo to see how much DP space we need.  17-Nov-90 DAL	lda #29	;Pass pointer to direct page.	jsr pushDirectPage	_ACEStartup	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start SANE.;===========================================startSANE	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	lda #10	;Pass pointer to direct page.	jsr pushDirectPage	_SANEStartup	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Pokey.;===========================================startPokey	PROC	ldx #$0221	; _StartVideoMix	jsl $E10000	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Print Manager.;===========================================startPrintMgr	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	pei <userID	;Pass application's user ID.	lda #19	;Pass pointer to direct page.	jsr pushDirectPage	_PMStartup	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Font Manager.;===========================================startFont	PROC	pei <userID	;Pass application's user ID.	lda #27	;Pass pointer to direct page.	jsr pushDirectPage	_FMStartup	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   Start Text Edit.;===========================================startTextEdit	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	pei <userID	;Pass application's user ID.	lda #34	;Pass pointer to direct page.	jsr pushDirectPage	_TEStartup	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   StartMidiSynth;===========================================;(Added 17-Nov-90 DAL)startMidiSynth	PROC	ldx #$0223	;_MidiSynthStartUp, or whatever it's called	jsl $e10000	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   StartAnimation;===========================================;(Added 17-Nov-90 DAL)startAnimation	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	pei <userID	;push the user ID!  19-Feb-91 DAL	lda #37	;Pass pointer to direct page.	jsr pushDirectPage	lda #0	pha	;ModeFlag=0	pha	;added 4-Dec-90 DAL (ModeFlag is really a LONG)	pha	;PatchTable=NIL	pha	;PatchTable=NIL	ldx #$0225	;_AnimStartUp	jsl $e10000	rts	ENDP;===========================================;   StartMediaCtl;===========================================;(Added 17-Nov-90 DAL)startMediaCtl	PROC	IMPORT pushDirectPage	pei <userID	;Pass application's user ID.	ldx #$0226	;_MCStartUp	jsl $e10000	rts	ENDP****************************************************************** Central handle disposing routine.  Inputs handle in a & x*** Inputs:*	a-reg low word of handle*	x-reg high word of handle** Outputs:*	a-reg error code*	carry error condition** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************KillIt	PROC	phx	pha	_DisposeHandle	rts	ENDP	END